<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Mapped, but served? Water, toilets and waste in Kibera and Mathare</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:wght@500;700&family=Source+Serif+4:wght@400;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.css">
<style>
:root{--ink:#12262c;--paper:#f2f5f5;--line:#c9d4d6;--water:#1670b5;--toilet:#c2410c;--waste:#6b7a1f;--muted:#4b6168}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
html,body{margin:0;height:100%}
body{font-family:"Source Serif 4",Georgia,serif;color:var(--ink);font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;background:#dfe7e8}
h1,h2{font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",system-ui,sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 .6em}
h1{font-size:2.3rem}h2{font-size:1.55rem}
#map{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:0}
#story{position:relative;z-index:2;width:min(440px,92vw);margin-left:4vw;pointer-events:none}
.chapter{min-height:100vh;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:6vh 0}
.card{pointer-events:auto;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:6px solid var(--ink);padding:1.4rem 1.5rem;border-radius:4px;box-shadow:0 2px 14px rgba(18,38,44,.18)}
.card p{margin:.6em 0}
.card small{color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-top:.8em;font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.4}
.chapter[data-layers*="water"] .card{border-left-color:var(--water)}
.chapter[data-layers*="toilets"]:not([data-layers*="water"]) .card{border-left-color:var(--toilet)}
.chapter[data-layers="waste"] .card{border-left-color:var(--waste)}
#legend{position:fixed;top:12px;right:12px;z-index:5;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:.6rem .8rem;font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.9rem;box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(18,38,44,.2)}
#legend label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin:.2rem 0;cursor:pointer}
#legend i{width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block;border:1px solid #fff;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ink)}
#legend .n{color:var(--muted);margin-left:auto;padding-left:.6rem}
#legend b{display:block;margin-bottom:.2rem}
a{color:var(--water)}
:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--toilet);outline-offset:2px}
@media (max-width:700px){
 body{font-size:17px}h1{font-size:1.8rem}
 #story{margin:0 auto}
 .chapter{align-items:flex-end;padding:4vh 0 6vh}
 #legend{top:8px;right:8px;font-size:.8rem;padding:.4rem .6rem}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{scroll-behavior:auto!important}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map" role="img" aria-label="Map of water points, toilets and waste points in Kibera and Mathare, Nairobi"></div>

<div id="legend" aria-label="Map layers">
  <b>Layers</b>
  <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="water" checked><i style="background:var(--water)"></i>Water points<span class="n" id="n-water"></span></label>
  <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="toilets" checked><i style="background:var(--toilet)"></i>Toilets<span class="n" id="n-toilets"></span></label>
  <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="waste" checked><i style="background:var(--waste)"></i>Waste points<span class="n" id="n-waste"></span></label>
</div>

<main id="story">

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.286,36.82,11" data-layers="">
 <div class="card">
  <h1>Mapped, but served?</h1>
  <p>Plans, budgets and services start from maps. When a settlement is missing from them, the people who live there are easy to leave out.</p>
  <p>This story map looks at water points, toilets and waste points in Kibera and Mathare, two settlements in Nairobi. Scroll to see what residents and mappers have recorded, and what the map cannot tell you.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.3133,36.7886,14" data-layers="">
 <div class="card">
  <h2>Kibera, a blank spot</h2>
  <p>Map Kibera describes Kibera as a blank spot on the map before its mapping project began in 2009. Without a map, there was little on paper to plan from.</p>
  <p>Residents began to map their own neighbourhood, and the result is open data that anyone can use.</p>
  <small>Source: Map Kibera Trust, its own account of its history.</small>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.2900,36.8240,12" data-layers="water">
 <div class="card">
  <h2>Water points</h2>
  <p>Each blue dot is a water point recorded on OpenStreetMap in Kibera or Mathare. Click a dot to see what was recorded about it.</p>
  <p>A dot tells you a water point was mapped. It does not tell you whether water is flowing today, what it costs, or who controls it.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.3133,36.7886,15" data-layers="water,toilets">
 <div class="card">
  <h2>Toilets</h2>
  <p>Orange dots are toilets. Some of this data may come from local mappers and some from larger facility-mapping efforts, so look at the source recorded in each popup.</p>
  <p>Where a status such as working or not working is recorded, it shows how current the information was when it was last checked, not how things are today.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.2600,36.8590,15" data-layers="water,toilets,waste">
 <div class="card">
  <h2>Waste points</h2>
  <p>Green dots are waste points in Mathare and Kibera. Waste is often the thinnest layer, because collection points are harder to define and keep up to date than a tap or a toilet.</p>
  <p>Compare the three layers using the legend. Where one layer is sparse, ask whether the service is missing or the mapping is.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.2900,36.8240,12" data-layers="water,toilets,waste">
 <div class="card">
  <h2>What being on the map does not do</h2>
  <p>Being mapped is the first step towards being planned for, but it does not guarantee a service. A map shows what is there, not what is fair, safe or affordable.</p>
  <p>Visibility can also expose people to risk. The question that matters is who controls the data, who decides what is shown, and who benefits from it.</p>
  <small>Research on Map Kibera, including Berdou (2011), raises questions about who participates in community mapping and who benefits.</small>
  <!-- Check Berdou (2011) in the original publication before you submit. -->
 </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" data-view="-1.2900,36.8240,12" data-layers="water,toilets,waste">
 <div class="card">
  <h2>About this map</h2>
  <p>Data: &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), including data mapped by Map Kibera Trust. Exported on [date].</p>
  <p>The map shows what has been mapped, not everything that exists. Points may be out of date or missing.</p>
  <p>Made by [Your name] for a KU Leuven master's course portfolio on counter-mapping and water and sanitation planning.</p>
  <!-- Add a line about Map Kibera's review only after they have checked the map. -->
 </div>
</section>

</main>

<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.js"></script>
<script>
(function(){
  var map = L.map('map',{zoomControl:true,preferCanvas:true,scrollWheelZoom:false}).setView([-1.286,36.82],11);
  L.tileLayer('https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',{
    maxZoom:19,
    attribution:'&copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors'
  }).addTo(map);
  map.zoomControl.setPosition('bottomright');

  var colors = {water:'#1670b5',toilets:'#c2410c',waste:'#6b7a1f'};
  var groups = {water:L.layerGroup(),toilets:L.layerGroup(),waste:L.layerGroup()};
  var counts = {water:0,toilets:0,waste:0};
  var areas = ['kibera','mathare'];
  var userHidden = {};

  function esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c];});}

  function popup(props, type){
    var p = props || {};
    if (p.tags && typeof p.tags === 'object') p = p.tags;
    var title = p.name || ({water:'Water point',toilets:'Toilet',waste:'Waste point'})[type];
    var skip = {'@id':1,id:1,'@geometry':1};
    var rows = Object.keys(p).filter(function(k){return !skip[k] && p[k] !== '' && p[k] !== null && typeof p[k] !== 'object';})
      .slice(0,14).map(function(k){return '<tr><td style="padding-right:.6rem;color:#4b6168">'+esc(k)+'</td><td>'+esc(p[k])+'</td></tr>';}).join('');
    return '<strong>'+esc(title)+'</strong>'+(rows?'<table style="font-size:.85rem;margin-top:.3rem">'+rows+'</table>':'<br>No details recorded.')+
      '<div style="font-size:.75rem;margin-top:.4rem;color:#4b6168">A point shows that something was mapped, not that it works today.</div>';
  }

  function load(type, area){
    return fetch('data/'+type+'_'+area+'.geojson')
      .then(function(r){ if(!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status); return r.json(); })
      .then(function(gj){
        var layer = L.geoJSON(gj,{
          pointToLayer:function(f,ll){return L.circleMarker(ll,{radius:6,color:'#fff',weight:1.5,fillColor:colors[type],fillOpacity:.9});},
          style:function(){return {color:colors[type],weight:2,fillOpacity:.35};},
          onEachFeature:function(f,l){counts[type]++; l.bindPopup(popup(f.properties,type));}
        });
        groups[type].addLayer(layer);
      })
      .catch(function(){ /* missing file: skip this layer */ });
  }

  var jobs = [];
  Object.keys(groups).forEach(function(t){ areas.forEach(function(a){ jobs.push(load(t,a)); }); });
  Promise.all(jobs).then(function(){
    Object.keys(counts).forEach(function(t){
      document.getElementById('n-'+t).textContent = counts[t] ? counts[t] : '0';
    });
  });

  function setLayers(list){
    Object.keys(groups).forEach(function(t){
      var cb = document.querySelector('input[data-layer="'+t+'"]');
      var want = list.indexOf(t) > -1 && !userHidden[t];
      cb.checked = list.indexOf(t) > -1 && !userHidden[t];
      if (want && !map.hasLayer(groups[t])) groups[t].addTo(map);
      if (!want && map.hasLayer(groups[t])) map.removeLayer(groups[t]);
    });
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('#legend input').forEach(function(cb){
    cb.addEventListener('change',function(){
      var t = cb.getAttribute('data-layer');
      userHidden[t] = !cb.checked;
      if (cb.checked) groups[t].addTo(map); else map.removeLayer(groups[t]);
    });
  });

  var chapters = document.querySelectorAll('.chapter');
  var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries){
    entries.forEach(function(e){
      if(!e.isIntersecting) return;
      var c = e.target;
      var v = c.getAttribute('data-view').split(',').map(Number);
      var layers = c.getAttribute('data-layers').split(',').filter(Boolean);
      userHidden = {};
      setLayers(layers);
      var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      if (reduce) map.setView([v[0],v[1]],v[2]); else map.flyTo([v[0],v[1]],v[2],{duration:1.4});
    });
  },{threshold:0.6});
  chapters.forEach(function(c){io.observe(c);});

  setLayers([]);
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
